   "C31": [
    "Decision 27 (Neil standing rule, 2026-10-08): this list IS the page /examples/animals (linked from SiteNav › Animals) - no list modal, no auto-open, no landing page. Add | Edit Animal opens as a routed modal over the page and closes back to it; Delete uses a confirmation modal. Decision 28 (Neil 18:46 BST): page_type Paginated Grid; tickets split into the page (T-ANIMAL-008: route, nav link, permission gate, no-permission message, layout, hosting the grid and the form modal) and the paginated grid (T-ANIMAL-003: columns, population, sorting, paging, row actions menu, empty state). Permissions (decision 22, Neil 2026-10-08 14:47 BST, supersedes decision 11; amended by decision 24, Neil 15:17 BST): animals have ONE permission of their own, animals_write (\"Manage animals\"), checked by policy AnimalsWrite on every animal endpoint (list, get, create, update, delete, form schema). No read permission. Decision 25: every user gets it through the Administrators and Standard groups (seeded); users outside those groups get it through group management (Q34). Animals are global (not per tenant). Row actions (decision 23, Neil 14:47 BST; amended by decision 26, Neil 15:17 BST): an Actions column at the end of the grid holding a row actions menu with Edit Animal and Delete Animal, built as a reusable, permission-aware grid feature in UI.NextJs.Framework (T-ANIMAL-007). View dropped (decision 20, Neil 2026-10-08 14:31 BST): no View Animal action and no View mode, and no read-only access (decision 24). Clicking a row does nothing (Q23). Decision 29 (Neil 19:04 BST via Review Bot): Is Furry and Has Hooves use the shared boolean-icon grid cell (green Check / red Close with Yes/No accessible names), not a read-only Switch. T-ANIMAL-009; Neil's own change, no re-approval. Decision 30 (Neil 19:57 BST, after his 19:52 dark-mode and 19:53 inverted-icon requests): each boolean cell is a filled circle - green for true, red for false - with Check / Close as a transparent cut-out (Icon knockout=\"circle\"; Neil 20:19). Light fills #609b44 / #ef5673, dark fills #8dc374 / #ff9aa8, via dedicated fill tokens; --app-boolean-glyph removed; --system-green / --system-red are unchanged. Last Amended maps to the platform audit columns UpdatedUtc (existing convention) and UpdatedBy (new user id column referencing auth.users). DB schema (decision 21, Neil 2026-10-08 14:35 BST): the Animal table lives in the new creatures schema (creatures.animals), not auth. Population sources use the entity name Animal; UpdatedBy → auth.users is a cross-schema FK (Q26). Same LoginDbContext, history table auth.__ef_migrations_history, no GRANTs, AddAnimals migration regenerated (Q24, Q25, Q27; accepted 15:44 BST).",
